Package: bicountbrms
Title: Joint Bivariate-Count brms Custom Families for Paired Counts
Version: 0.10.0
Date: 2026-09-01
Authors@R:
    person("Adam N. H.", "Smith", , "anhsmith@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0059-6206"))
Description: Provides custom brms families for comparing two paired count
    sources, modelling the pair jointly via trivariate reduction rather than
    reducing it to a difference. Two families are supplied: a bivariate
    Poisson (bipois) and its overdispersed bivariate Negative-Binomial sibling
    (binegbin). Each has a second constructor (bipois_partialobs,
    binegbin_partialobs) that admits rows on which the first count was never
    recorded, scoring them by the integrated-out marginal of the same joint
    model, so those rows still inform the shared component and the second
    source. Modelling the pair rather than its difference captures the overall
    level, the correlation between sources, and marginal overdispersion
    alongside the disagreement, and supports simulating one count conditional
    on the other, including on rows where it was never recorded. An
    interpretable reparameterisation separates overall level, congruence, and
    source bias, giving each a finite null and so admitting
    penalised-complexity priors. The Negative-Binomial family lets the two
    source-specific components differ in overdispersion.
